        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>What Wildlife Will I See?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Khao Sok National Park is one of Southeast Asia’s <a href="https://www.worldwildlife.org/resources/explainers/what-is-biodiversity/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">biodiversity</a> treasures. It’s estimated to contain over 5% of all known species on Earth!
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 my-6 pl-2">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong>Mammals:</strong> Long-tailed macaques, pig-tailed macaques, stump-tailed macaques, dusky langurs, and gibbons. Rarely, tapirs, wild boars or wild elephants are spotted near the water’s edge.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong>Birds:</strong> Over 300 species, including hornbills, kingfishers, and broadbills — a paradise for birdwatchers.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong>Reptiles & Amphibians:</strong> 170+ snake species (mostly nocturnal), monitor lizards, frogs and toads.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong>Insects:</strong> Expect tropical abundance — Along with mosquitoes, dragonflies, beetles, spiders, and ants wonder at dazzling butterflies or the enormous Atlas moth (wingspan up to 30 cm).</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[#223e2c] text-base leading-relaxed">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#7a5813]/70 mt-2.5 flex-shrink-0"></span>
            <span><strong>Fish:</strong> Carp, catfish, perch, and snakeheads thrive here — you’ll often see them around the raft houses in the crystal clear water.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
